Seven rigid gap genotypes

For exactly the following non-twin gap sizes, the endpoint-safe local residue system leaves no optional carrier inside the gap:

[
g\in{4,6,8,10,12,16,20}.
]

Their carrier loads are fixed for every eligible prime pair:

|Gap|Fixed load|
|--:|---------:|
|4  |(1)       |
|6  |(0)       |
|8  |(1/3)     |
|10 |(1/2)     |
|12 |(1/5)     |
|16 |(3/7)     |
|20 |(1/3)     |

Why only these seven? Factor (3) is forced or excluded by (h\bmod3), never optional. Variation first becomes possible when a prime (r\ge5), not dividing (h), has a matching-parity multiple inside the radius: (x=r<h) for odd (h), or (x=2r<h) for even (h). The seven radii (h\in{2,3,4,5,6,8,10}) are exactly those without such an optional carrier. For larger radii, an elementary primorial/Bertrand argument supplies one.

