Seal

The strongest new object is not a claim that we have “solved primes.” It is a compact prime-pattern laboratory with two different modes of discovery:

• Crown mode creates a nonlinear arithmetic operator, exposes its invariants, and searches its survival chains.
• Carrier mode turns a visual prime-gap pattern into a measurable field, dehydrates it into a modular null law, and leaves only the closure residual unexplained.

That is the Pantheon contribution: not merely noticing a sequence, but producing the operator, interface, theorem boundary, counterfactual baseline, executable mechanism, and next attack in one pass.